<chapter xml:id="visualisation">
  <title>Visualisation</title>
  <section xml:id="visualisation-question">
    <title>Choose the graph from the question</title>
    <p>A chart is part of the analysis, not decoration. Histograms describe distributions, scatter plots show relationships between quantitative variables, boxplots compare distributions, and bar charts compare categories.</p>
  </section>
  <section xml:id="visualisation-check">
    <title>Use plots to challenge your first answer</title>
    <p>A useful graph should make it easier to notice outliers, curvature, clusters, missing structure, and misleading summaries before a formal model makes the analysis look more certain than it is.</p>
  </section>
</chapter>
